    "criterion_order": [
      "Navigate Xbox.com to the 'Best sellers' section",
      "Open a product page for a game from 'Best sellers'",
      "Report publisher, developer, and release date from the product page",
      "Respect constraints (no sign-in; no purchase or download; stop after recording details)"
    ],
    "criterion_descriptions": [
      "Use Xbox.com (starting from https://www.xbox.com/en-US/ is acceptable) and make a reasonable attempt to locate the “Best sellers” section (or equivalent clearly best-selling list) on Xbox.com. Full credit if the agent reaches the Best sellers area OR if Xbox.com prevents access/visibility due to uncontrollable blockers (e.g., site not loading, CAPTCHA, region/age gating, persistent cookie/consent overlay, A/B layout where Best sellers is not present) and the agent clearly reports the blocker and what was attempted. Partial credit if the agent finds a comparable best-selling list that is not clearly labeled “Best sellers” when “Best sellers” is not readily discoverable.",
      "Select any one game shown in the “Best sellers” list (or closest equivalent best-selling list found) and open its product page on Xbox.com. Full credit if the opened page is clearly the product page for a game that was presented in the Best sellers list. If opening the product page is blocked by uncontrollable factors (e.g., age/region gating, repeated redirects, site errors), full credit if the agent demonstrates a reasonable attempt and clearly reports the blocker. Partial credit if a product page is opened on Xbox.com but traceability to Best sellers is unclear due to page changes or missing context.",
      "From the opened game product page, record and report the game’s publisher, developer, and release date as displayed on Xbox.com (including within expandable sections like “Details”/“More information” if present). Full credit if all three fields are correctly captured. If one or more of these fields are not shown/are unavailable on the product page due to Xbox.com content differences, locale/region, or gating, full credit if the agent clearly states which fields are missing/unavailable and does not fabricate. Partial credit if only 2 of 3 are reported when the third is visible, or if there are minor transcription errors.",
      "Comply with constraints by not signing in and not buying or downloading anything, and stop after opening the product page and recording publisher/developer/release date (or reporting unavailability of those fields). Full credit if the agent avoids sign-in and avoids completing any purchase/download flows and stops promptly after collecting required info. Partial credit if the agent navigates near purchase/download CTAs or unavoidable interstitials appear but no transaction/download/sign-in is initiated or completed. No credit if the agent signs in or initiates/completes a purchase or download."
    ],
